{
  "id": "h13",
  "order": 13,
  "title": "Leaps to a far key",
  "summary": "Reach for a far key and come back, the move behind La Campanella's bell.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "The bell",
      "body": "La Campanella means \"the little bell\". The right hand keeps playing one high note, the bell, between the notes of the tune, so it is always reaching up and coming back.\n\nA move to a key far from the last one is a **leap**.\n\n**Why it matters:** a leap is aimed with the eyes before the hand goes. Look at the landing key, then move. Practise slowly until you hit it every time; speed comes later.\n\nHere the bell is the top C on your keyboard. Press **Watch**: the thumb plays the tune, the little finger plays the bell.",
